
           AVH-BaudCheck V0.1 For DayDream BBS - Quick documentation
           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

  What is this thing?
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  AVH-BaudCheck is a tool which allows the sysop to don't allow users with
  low baud connect to enter into the bbs except some users who have the
  password to enter.

  Features
  ~~~~~~~~
	- 100% DDDoor!
	- password protection for low-baud rates
  - ugly design! ;)

  Installation
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~
	1) Copy all files from this archive to their specific directory

	2) Edit the AVH-BaudCheck.cfg to your needs:
     1. line: min. bps rate (max. 7 chars!)
     2. line: password for lower bps rates (max. 20 chars, NOT CASESENSITIVE!)

     ===================================================================
     WARNING: the config file MUST be located in "DayDream:Configs/" !!!
              i'm not using the env-variable!!!
     ===================================================================

  3) Add following line to your DayDream:Data/FrontEnds.DAT
     --- cut here ---
     Doors:AVH-BaudCheck %N
     --- cut here ---
     It should be the FIRST line in your FrontEnds.DAT !!!

  Usage
  ~~~~~
  Login to your BBS and see...
  Set the min. bps rate something >60000 and you can try out your password!
  Don't forget to set min. bps rate back after testing it! ;)

